From: Tabor SPE toolchain project
Subject: powerpcspe: use actual backchain for PIC return address at depth zero

Candidate against pinned GCC8.5.0. The active gnuspe backend is powerpcspe,
not rs6000. Mirror the count-zero frame correction present in the same
archive's gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c: the generic frame pointer addresses
locals when FRAME_GROWS_DOWNWARD (stack protection), not the backchain.
Use stack_pointer_rtx at depth zero; retain existing nonzero-depth behavior.
This preserves stack protection and changes no other target backend.
Validation: protected PIC reproducer and fresh libc unwind tests required.

--- a/gcc/config/powerpcspe/powerpcspe.c
+++ b/gcc/config/powerpcspe/powerpcspe.c
@@ -28073,5 +28073,10 @@
       cfun->machine->ra_needs_full_frame = 1;
 
+      /* FRAME names locals rather than the backchain when stack protection
+         makes FRAME_GROWS_DOWNWARD true.  Depth zero needs the real SP.  */
+      if (count == 0)
+        frame = stack_pointer_rtx;
+
       return
 	gen_rtx_MEM
 	  (Pmode,
